%S A400514 1,4,25,3,174,60,1481,1103,1,14136,22174,16,149490,496395,519,1
%N A400514 Irregular triangle read by rows: T(k,d) is the number of nonisomorphic prime k-element posets (no nontrivial modules) of order dimension exactly d, where k >= 4 and 2 <= d <= floor(k/2).
%C A400514 The order dimension of a poset P is the least number of linear extensions whose intersection is P.
%H A400514 B. I. Bayoumi et al., <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/0012-365X(94)90370-0">Counting two-dimensional posets</a>, Discrete Mathematics 131 (1994), 29-37.
%H A400514 B. I. Bayoumi et al., <a href="https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Soheir-M-Khamis/publication/266355942_On_recognizing_the_dimension_of_a_poset/links/5a2bcc14aca2728e05deb209/On-recognizing-the-dimension-of-a-poset.pdf">On recognizing the dimension of a poset</a>, Journal of the Egyptian Mathematical Society 6(1) (1998), 1-8, Table 1.
%H A400514 Elisha Goldman, <a href="/A400514/a400514.py.txt">Simple enumeration</a>
%F A400514 Sum_{d=2..floor(k/2)} T(k,d) = A354693(k) for k >= 4.
%e A400514 The triangle begins (row k lists dimensions d=2,...,floor(k/2)):
%e A400514 k\d       2       3    4  5
